                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b8f5f931-9861-3f3c-ae65-b40a6acba35a",
                        "entry_id": "2668b679-e19b-349f-a928-8ab80c5ac1ba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Aversion ou haine contre les personnes aromantiques."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a7de75c-c378-4f14-a100-bbc911db9e11",
                                "sense_id": "b8f5f931-9861-3f3c-ae65-b40a6acba35a",
                                "text": "Le A n'est pas pour les alliés mais bien pour les personnes aromantiques (et aussi asexuelles), qui font entièrement partie de la communauté, ne sont pas conformes à l'amatonormativité et subissent l'arophobie qui est une oppression spécifique."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e1635c5-5b26-4a91-beb0-a9ccefeefb49",
                                "sense_id": "b8f5f931-9861-3f3c-ae65-b40a6acba35a",
                                "text": "L’oppression subie par les personnes aromantiques, s’appelle l’arophobie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d08c6647-b129-4d20-a82e-aa567f3d9755",
                                "sense_id": "b8f5f931-9861-3f3c-ae65-b40a6acba35a",
                                "text": "Comme l’homophobie dont souffre la population homosexuelle, l’arophobie peut concerner l’aromantique qui doit subir, encore et encore, les commentaires de la famille et des amis. Avec cette éternelle question subie : ‘Alors ? Pas encore trouvé l’amour ?’"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5ffc5e1b-f582-49d2-95bb-e5c38ebf89f6",
                        "source_entry_id": "2668b679-e19b-349f-a928-8ab80c5ac1ba",
                        "source_sense_id": "b8f5f931-9861-3f3c-ae65-b40a6acba35a",
                        "target_lang_word": "arophobia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "arophobia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5f1f79ac-2047-3880-bc1c-4be6750252dc",
                                        "entry_id": "3577ebc2-f7d9-368e-9be9-9c2392a14c76",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fear, dislike, or hatred of aromantic people and/or aromanticism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "neologism",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "583df6da-3e7c-4319-996a-f5258438bbb2",
                                                "sense_id": "5f1f79ac-2047-3880-bc1c-4be6750252dc",
                                                "text": "Even in situations where one's identity is accepted completely, there can still be lingering doubts derived from internalized acephobia and arophobia or from a wider sense of otherness from general society or even other members of the community."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "827e2b57-38df-4122-b4ff-a91c6ab9a3ad",
                                                "sense_id": "5f1f79ac-2047-3880-bc1c-4be6750252dc",
                                                "text": "This leads to a society that is rife wih m-spec phobia, arophobia and acephobia and erasure that can be internalized, causing people to struggle with their identity, which can greatly impact their mental health."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf5fa2ad-eec7-4f49-b057-499e715fca1e",
                                                "sense_id": "5f1f79ac-2047-3880-bc1c-4be6750252dc",
                                                "text": "Comments like those listed above, especially comments such as 'you're just depressed' or 'you're cold and heartless' are arguably a big contributor to internalized arophobia."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
